---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SkipLink from '../../components/SkipLink.astro';
import SiteNav from '../../components/SiteNav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Definition of done — Kala docs"
  description="Understand Kala's quality gates, STEP validation, and what 'done' means for a CAD part."
>
  <SkipLink />
  <SiteNav />
  <main id="main-content" class="doc-page">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <nav class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/docs">Docs</a> / Definition of done
        </nav>
        <h1>Definition of done</h1>
        
        <p>
          A CAD part generated by Kala is considered "done" when it passes all quality gates and produces a valid STEP file
          that can be opened, inspected, and modified in standard CAD systems.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Quality gates</h2>
        
        <h3>Geometry validation</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>All features successfully constructed via FreeCAD API calls</li>
          <li>No broken or invalid geometry</li>
          <li>All dimensions within specified tolerances</li>
          <li>No self-intersecting surfaces</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Constraint satisfaction</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>All specified constraints met (dimensions, clearances, mounting points)</li>
          <li>Part fits within defined envelope or space</li>
          <li>Mating features align correctly</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>STEP file compliance</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Valid STEP AP203 or AP214 format</li>
          <li>Can be opened in target CAD systems without errors</li>
          <li>Geometry metadata preserved</li>
          <li>No data loss in export</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>What "done" does NOT include</h2>
        <p>
          Kala's definition of done is focused on technical correctness and file validity, not subjective metrics:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>No benchmark scores or pass rates (metrics stay internal)</li>
          <li>No aesthetic or stylistic evaluation</li>
          <li>No cost optimization unless explicitly specified in brief</li>
          <li>No manufacturing process selection</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Rejection criteria</h2>
        <p>
          A part is rejected and not delivered if:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>STEP file is invalid or cannot be opened</li>
          <li>Critical dimensions are outside tolerance</li>
          <li>Specified constraints are violated</li>
          <li>Geometry contains errors or degeneracies</li>
        </ul>
        
        <p>
          When a part is rejected, Kala will report the specific validation failure and attempt a rebuild if possible.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc-page {
    padding: var(--section-padding-desktop) 0;
    min-height: calc(100vh - var(--nav-height) - 20rem);
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    display: block;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }

  .prose {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .prose h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .prose h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose ul, .prose ol {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .doc-page {
      padding: var(--section-padding-mobile) 0;
    }
  }
</style>
